    "summary": "I built a three-storey tower and it passes the checks: no rule errors and the mesh-collision check reads \"clear\". It's two columns side by side, at cells (0,0) and (1,0). Each column is three north-half bases stacked on levels 0–2, with snaps between the storeys. Half bases were needed because drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base. A half base can only carry the same kind above it, so every storey is a half base too. Each column has one drawer on the bottom storey and an open full-depth bin on the top storey. A single column would only take one drawer, so I used two to get more than one. The two columns aren't joined: the configurator offered no joint-bolt places. The middle storey is left empty, and 22 outer faces are open with no caps or covers."
  },
